<title>ESTONIA: INTERBANK RATES RISE SLIGHTLY.</title>
<headline>INTERBANK RATES RISE SLIGHTLY.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central bank's weekly</p>
<p>settings of Estonian interbank rates, Talibor and Talibid,</p>
<p>showed a slight rise on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bid/offer in all periods rose, with one-week up at</p>
<p>4.97/3.97 versus 4.85/3.85 last week.</p>
<p>		One-wk/previous  One-month/pvs  Three-month/pvs</p>
<p> TALIBOR    4.97/4.85	  6.57/6.43	8.05/8.02</p>
<p> TALIBID    3.97/3.85	  5.57/5.43	7.05/7.02</p>
<p>The rates are next published on March 26</p>
<p>-- Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
